			"Message": "docs(Mist): Expand README with comprehensive technical documentation\n\nRestore detailed technical documentation to the Mist README, replacing the condensed benefit-focused version with full API docs, architecture diagrams, usage examples, and integration guides.\n\nKey additions:\n- Expanded Key Features section listing Hickory DNS, authoritative zone, DNSSEC support\n- Architecture section with ASCII diagram showing layered component structure\n- DNS Zone Configuration documenting editor.land zone and forward allowlist\n- Usage section with Rust code examples for starting server, getting port, creating resolvers\n- Dependencies section listing all crate versions\n- Security Considerations covering isolation, allowlist, DNSSEC, loopback binding\n- Integration section explaining how Mountain, Air, SideCar, and Cocoon use Mist\n- Building & Testing section with cargo commands\n\nThis provides developers with the complete technical reference needed to understand and integrate Mist's DNS isolation capabilities.",
